W2 Negative forecast means for a count
W3 The standard error does not grow with the forecast level as a count's variance does
W4 Systematic multi-step bias: over-prediction at high forecast levels and in November-April, under-prediction in the June-July onset
W5 Reporting-regime breaks in the test years that no province's own history predicts
W6 The specification was a first default, not a selected one
